{"name":"Glaucous","hex":"#6082b6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"glaucous","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a pale grey or bluish-green, especially when covered with a powdery residue.","Covered with a bloom or a pale powdery covering, regardless of colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glaucous"}],"entries":[{"title":"Glaucous","blocks":[{"text":"Glaucous is used to describe the pale grey or bluish-green appearance of the surfaces of some plants, as well as in the names of birds, such as the glaucous gull, glaucous-winged gull, glaucous macaw, and glaucous tanager."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glaucous","wikidata":"Q310115"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Close_up_grapes.jpg/120px-Close_up_grapes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Close_up_grapes.jpg/250px-Close_up_grapes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Close_up_grapes.jpg/120px-Close_up_grapes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClose_up_grapes.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Plums.jpg/120px-Plums.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Plums.jpg/250px-Plums.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Plums.jpg/120px-Plums.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APlums.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Sedum_spathulifolium_4916.JPG/120